<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Ascania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ascanians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Ascania is a German princely dynasty named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschersleben">Aschersleben</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> founded the Margraviate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1157, and his descendants ruled it until the line died out in 1320, extending German settlement east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. Other branches held the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and Anhalt, where they ruled until 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-ascania.jpg" alt="House of Ascania" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glasshouse with elements by Sodacan and Trondivers · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_the_Duchy_of_Anhalt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
